WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.569
-Thank you very much. Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.871
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.139
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.741
Well, guys,
we are now officially

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.310
one week
into Joe Biden's presidency,

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.012
and for the first time
in a while,

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:15.281
a week actually felt
like a week.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.718
-[ Laughs ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.287
Yep, Biden's already been
in office for a week.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.090
Time sure does fly
when you're not doom-scrolling

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.459
through Twitter till 4:00 a.m.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:27.960
Right now,
liquor stores are like,

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.529
"Where the hell
did everybody go? Hey!"

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.097
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.432
In one week,
we've gone from insurrection

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:34.867
to cool and collected,

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.502
anarchy to no malarkey,

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.271
drinking bleach
to boring speech.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.640
You know, it's been a ride.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.611
I'll take it.
And this is interesting --

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.780
even though Biden has only been
on the job for seven full days,

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.217
his initial approval rating is
higher than Trump's ever was.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.752
-Ah.
-Whoo!

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.453
Yeah.
I'm pretty sure, by the end,

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:56.222
Trump's approval rating
was hovering around

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.459
the temperature that you have to
store the Pfizer vaccine.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.127
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.962
Meanwhile, Trump was like,
"Yeah.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.264
But if you ask militia members
on the no-fly list,

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:06.533
my numbers
are through the roof."

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.203
Well, Rudy Giuliani
is back in the headlines again

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:13.773
with more bad news.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.042
YouTube just confirmed
that they're suspended --

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.410
they have suspended Rudy
from making money

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.814
off the ads
that play before his videos.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.217
I didn't even know
Rudy was on YouTube.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.718
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.087
Let's take a look at what
he's doing over there.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.656
-If you want a good cigar,
go to a good cigar shop.

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.158
-[ Laughing ] What?

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.393
-If you want the best,
go to Famous Smoke Shop.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:37.597
American Hartford Gold
is the company you can trust

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.632
when it comes to buying gold.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.469
Order Omega XL now
and get a second bottle free.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.238
Earbuds from Raycon --

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.807
because they connect
my Bluetooth seamlessly

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.041
and you're
not having to untangle...

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.210
-What?!
-Wait.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.678
...all these headphone wires.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.913
-Wait. Quick question.
-Is that real?

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.482
-Quick question --

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:58.317
who's buying earbuds 'cause
Rudy Giuliani recommends them?

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.987
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That was real?

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.021
-Yeah, it's real.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.490
-For real?
-That's real.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.758
Seriously,
what happened to Rudy?

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.926
I mean,
he's gone from QAnon to QVC.

00:02:07.926 --> 00:02:10.129
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:11.597
Apparently,
Rudy's so desperate for cash,

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:14.033
he's gonna let Exxon start
drilling his head for oil.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.268
-Ohh!
-Wow.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.702
-Actually,
I don't know if it's true.

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:19.973
that's what I heard.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.541
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.609
Oh, some business news --
this is a good one here --

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:27.880
today, Kraft Heinz announced
its new pink, candy-flavored

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.949
macaroni and cheese
for Valentine's Day.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.083
-Hm.
-Take a look at this.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.186
-Oh, my God.
-Oh, God!

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:35.220
-Mmm. Candy-flavored pasta.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.156
[ Italian accent ]
Just like Mama used to make.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.524
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.225
[ Normal voice ] Even
the Olive Garden looked at that

00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:41.794
and said,
"Ah, that ain't right."

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.796
[ Laughter ]
Can we see it again?

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.197
-Mnh-mnh.
-No.

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:48.668
-I'm 99% sure that's what
custodians throw on the floor

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:49.969
after a kid barfs.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.873
[ Laughter ]
I -- I -- I -- I -- I --

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.742
Can we just see it one qu--
I just got to look at it again.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.210
Yeah.
-Ew.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.746
-They even have a good name
for it -- Pepto-Bis-Mac.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.214
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.083
But this is funny --
so, later this year,

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.718
the Postal Service
is going to release

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.387
a new series of
"Star Wars" stamps.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:11.857
I never thought I'd have to lick
C-3PO to pay my cable bill,

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:15.861
but here we are.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.930
When he saw the news,
Jimmy Carter was like,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.265
"I've never been on a stamp,
but by all means,

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:21.701
let's give one to R2-D2."

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.970
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.072
Well, this is exciting --

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.007
Six Flags Great Adventure
in New Jersey

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.342
just finished the track

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:33.212
for its 130-foot-high
Jersey Devil Coaster.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:34.513
And when it opens,

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.649
it'll be the world's tallest,
fastest, and longest

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.618
single-rail coaster.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.119
Of course,
since it's New Jersey,

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.288
your hair's got to be
this tall to ride.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.257
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:47.193
[ Applause ]

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.895
It's nice that
they added a new roller coaster.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.063
The other roller coasters
in that park are so old,

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:52.398
they still have ashtrays.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.437
"[Exhales sharply]
Does this thing go upside down?"

00:03:57.437 --> 00:04:00.039
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.774
Get this -- I read that,
'cause of the pandemic,

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.543
New Yorkers can now order
scratch-off tickets online

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:07.246
and have them delivered
right to their house.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.315
I'm not --
I'm not sure I love this idea.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.916
One of my favorite
New York traditions

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.418
was waiting in line
with my lunch

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.187
while the guy ahead of me took
15 minutes to pick out tickets.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:16.823
"Give me the three Lucky 7's.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:19.458
I'll do, uh, two Birthday Bucks.

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:22.528
I want the, uh,
BOGGLE Cashword

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:25.832
and, uhhh...
five Tic Tac Snows."

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.401
"Well, you touched
the sixth one.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.736
Give me six of them.
Why not?"

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.470
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.540
"Go with sixes --
that's the secret.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.475
These are scratch-offs.

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:39.212
Every sixth one is a winner."

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.980
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.616
"But that's the fourth one,
so give me two more.

00:04:44.616 --> 00:04:46.752
Give me eight tickets.

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:48.688
And that starts the six again."

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.123
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.190
What?

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:54.327
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:55.962
And finally,
some news from overseas --

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:59.899
China has rolled out
an anal swab coronavirus test...

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.867
-Ohh, ohh, come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:05.204
-...saying it's more accurate
than the throat method.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.039
It's more accurate,
but it's still being called

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.976
the number-two test.
-Ah!

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:14.147
[ Drums play ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.781
And for even more accuracy,

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:18.150
they do a nasal swab
and an anal swab

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.386
until they touch in the middle.
-No! Aah!

